# API Design Conventions

## Resource URLs

```
GET    /products              → list all products
GET    /products/:id          → get product with aggregated rating
GET    /products/:id/reviews  → list reviews for a product
POST   /products/:id/reviews  → create a review (auth required)
PUT    /reviews/:id           → edit own review (auth required)
DELETE /reviews/:id           → delete own review (auth required)
POST   /auth/register         → register
POST   /auth/login            → login, sets refresh cookie
POST   /auth/refresh          → exchange refresh cookie for new access token
POST   /auth/logout           → clears refresh cookie
```

## HTTP Status Codes

| Situation | Code |
|---|---|
| Successful creation | 201 |
| Successful read/update | 200 |
| Unauthenticated | 401 |
| Authenticated but not authorized (not your review) | 403 |
| Resource not found | 404 |
| Unique constraint violation (duplicate review) | 409 |
| Validation error | 422 |

## Response Shape

Successful list response:
```json
{ "data": [...], "meta": { "total": 42 } }
```

Successful single-item response:
```json
{ "data": { ... } }
```

Error response:
```json
{ "error": { "code": "DUPLICATE_REVIEW", "message": "You already reviewed this product." } }
```

## Validation

Validate all request bodies at the controller/route level before they reach service logic.
Use class-validator (NestJS) or Zod/Joi (Express) — whichever matches the chosen framework.

## Auth Middleware

Protected routes must use an `authenticate` middleware that verifies the JWT access token
and attaches `req.user` (or sets the NestJS request context). Never check auth inside service methods.
